From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps5cemu <ps5cemu@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:33:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PS5: the first-person body faces the view again, and the root
 latch only fills a skipped frame; built, untested on console

The camera hook built a player matrix from the camera's own rotation, so the headset's model-space yaw lost the player model's axis, and ExtractPlayerBodyYaw's fixed 180 left Skl_Root 180 degrees from the view: on the console the body faced away while walking. Skl_Root is posed from the live player matrix and the fresh reference matrix again, as in 0.5.0. The last good root is still written on a frame whose actor, model, hand pose or bone is skipped, and its once-a-second line stays.
---
 src/game/botw/camera/camera.cpp   | 41 ++-----------------------------
 src/game/botw/camera/camera.h     |  9 -------
 src/game/botw/player/skeleton.cpp | 40 +++++-------------------------
 3 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 82 deletions(-)

